          <change when="2022-01-28T05:47:54-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Vote - AcceptText - Ὡ̣ρίων is good. \δευ/τέρου ditto. | Change all BGU references in ed. to BL 1.14.</change>
          <change when="2022-01-23T16:48:58-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/Mike%20Sampson">Vote - DEFER - We can certainly say that no square brackets are needed, and although I agree that omega is better than alpha, I would note that rho elsewhere in this text tends to descend straight down.The only parallel for this swooping one is at the beginning of l. 7, where I would also suggest we read &lt;:&lt;:\δευ/τέρου|subst|τερου:&gt;=PN C.M. Sampson (from photo)|ed|δευτέρου:&gt;.  In concert, the proposed reading is superior, and I defer largely so that another set of eyes can confirm my proposal.</change>
          <change when="2022-01-23T11:22:33-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Vote - AcceptText - The open round curve just before the hole in the papyrus and the sinusoid ink trace to the right of the hole do indeed fit the reading Ὡ̣ρίων far better than the previous [Ἀ]πίωνι̣.</change>
